e checkout's own data is never touched)."},"adopt-edition":{"bootstrap":"before","flags":["--help","--cwd","--non-interactive","--json"],"effects":"Add edition.json and sources.lock.json for the existing tracked local source, preserving declared project identity and existing copy/composition records. Create an empty base-copies.json only when none exists. Review and stage the new authoring inputs; no source regeneration, install setup or commit."},"refresh-base":{"bootstrap":"before","flags":["--help","--cwd","--non-interactive","--json","--ref","--base","--base-archive","--from-api","--record","--offline","--edition-migration"],"effects":"Consent to each declared edition edit with repeatable --edition-migration ID; refresh leaves the edit owed. Refresh recorded Base copies to --ref FULL_COMMIT, preserving acknowledged adaptations and applied migrations; announce removed singleton retirement. Deliver invoked workflow helpers atomically; adopt tracked known historical Verify templates and preserve divergent workflows with adoption notices. Acquire committed source from the declared Base repository (default https://github.com/runeditrun/base.git), or read immutable trees, blobs and ancestry through authenticated gh with --from-api, or use --base CHECKOUT or --base-archive DIRECTORY with --ref FULL_COMMIT for an exported source tree. --offline requires --base or --base-archive and never acquires remote source. Refuse incomplete Git checkouts without changing their records. Review the diff and run edition tests before committing."},"signin":{"flags":["--help","--cwd","--non-interactive","--json","--environment","--env-file"],"effects":"A one-time sign-in link for the hosted owner, without mail. Uses the Cloudflare credentials that deployed --environment (default production; from the environment or --env-file) to write a single-use grant for the recorded owner into that deployment's auth database, then prints the link once to this terminal; it is never saved. The link works once, only for that owner, expires within 15 minutes, and its use is recorded in the owner's audit log. Signed in this way, the owner can correct a wrong email in settings."}},"aliases":{"setup":"setup","dev":"dev","preview":"preview","build":"build","verify":"verify","reset":"reset","deploy":"deploy","export":"export","import":"import","doctor":"doctor","describe":"describe","check":"check","release":"release","deps":"install","rer":null},"local":{"state":".wrangler/state","settings":[".dev.vars",".dev.vars.previous"],"installerState":".seed/installer","prepared":false,"ownerSaved":false,"origin":null,"devIdentity":true,"devKey":".rer/local/dev-key.env"},"door":{"protocol":1},"repositoryCommands":{"install":{"usage":"rer install <repo> [--dir DIR] [FLAGS]","effects":"Install rer for this user, clone or reuse the repository, install its dependencies, then stop."},"setup":{"usage":"rer setup <repo> [--dir DIR] [FLAGS]","effects":"Install rer, clone or reuse the repository, install dependencies and set up a local owner, then print the dev command."},"dev":{"usage":"rer dev <repo> [--dir DIR] [FLAGS]","effects":"Install rer, clone or reuse the repository, install and set up as needed, then start dev and print RER_READY and RER_OPEN."}}}
